{"paragraphs":[{"text":"%md\n# About This Lab\n**Objective:** Be able to use User Defined Functions (UDFs) to transform DataFrames\n**File locations:**\n**Successful outcome:**\n**Before you begin:**\n**Related lessons:** Working with DataFrames\n\nCopyright © 2010–2021 Cloudera. All rights reserved.\nNot to be reproduced or shared without prior written consent from Cloudera.\n\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorHide":true,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195690_1929965650","id":"20171105-200834_1116095891","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"focus":true,"$$hashKey":"object:1387"},{"text":"%md\n## Overview\n\nIn this module we demonstrate how to create and apply user-defined functions.\n\n\n## User-Defined Functions\n\n* It is relatively easy to create and apply a user-defined function (UDF)\n    * Define a Scala function that operates on a row of data\n    * Register the Scala function as a UDF and specify the return type\n    * Apply the UDF as if it were a built-in function\n\n* Scala and any required packages must be installed on the worker nodes\n    * It is possible to distribute required packages via Spark\n\n* Built-in functions are more efficient than user-defined functions\n    * Use built-in functions when available\n    * Create user-defined functions only when necessary","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195692_-380509600","id":"20210610-041300_636880277","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:40:59-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1388"},{"text":"%md\n# Setup\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:00-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195694_1729026810","id":"20181114-164229_902436001","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:00-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:00-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1389"},{"title":"Read the raw ride data from HDF and clean it","text":"%spark\n\nval rides = spark.read.option(\"header\",\"true\").option(\"inferSchema\",\"true\").csv(\"/duocar/raw/rides/\")\n\n// Cast `date_time` to a timestamp:\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{col}\n\nval rides_clean = rides.withColumn(\"date_time\", col(\"date_time\").cast(\"timestamp\"))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:00-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195695_1608878544","id":"20210610-041458_574907270","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:00-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1390"},{"text":"%md\n# Lesson\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195696_1583162251","id":"20210609-150445_381117564","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1391"},{"text":"%md\n## Example 1: Hour of Day","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195698_-1425563997","id":"20210610-041602_390464956","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:45-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1392"},{"title":"Define the Scala function","text":"%spark\n\nimport java.sql.Timestamp\ndef hour_of_day(time: Timestamp) : Int = return time.getHours ","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:45-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195699_-316086129","id":"20210610-041616_689400131","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:45-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1393"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nThe Spark `TimestampType` corresponds to Scala `java.sql.Timestamp` objects.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195700_640298960","id":"20210610-041801_1207629809","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1394"},{"title":"Test the Scala function","text":"%spark\n\nval dt = new Timestamp(2017, 7, 21, 5, 51, 10,0)\nhour_of_day(dt)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195701_764212663","id":"20210610-041853_1273796548","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:47-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:49-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1395"},{"title":"Register the Scala function as a UDF","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{udf}\n\n//val hour_of_day_udf = udf(hour_of_day(_)) // Error (missing parameter type for expanded function)\n\nval hour_of_day_udf = udf((dt: Timestamp) => hour_of_day(dt))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:49-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195703_351729299","id":"20210610-041937_709330143","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:50-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:52-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1396"},{"title":"Apply the UDF","text":"%spark\n\nrides_clean.select($\"date_time\", hour_of_day_udf($\"date_time\")).show(5, false)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:52-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195704_-1559297599","id":"20210610-042028_341706402","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:52-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:41:54-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1397"},{"title":"Use the UDF to compute the number of rides by hour of day","text":"%spark\n\n(rides_clean\n  .select(hour_of_day_udf($\"date_time\").alias(\"hour_of_day\"))\n  .groupBy(\"hour_of_day\")\n  .count()\n  .orderBy(\"hour_of_day\")\n  .show(25))","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:41:54-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195705_741580395","id":"20210610-042204_1273871975","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:41:54-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1398"},{"text":"%md\n## Example 2: Great-Circle Distance\n\nThe [great-circle distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great-circle_distance) is the shortest distance between two points on the surface of a sphere. \nIn this example we create a user-defined function to compute the [haversine approximation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haversine_formula) to the great-circle distance between the ride origin and destination.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195707_1760237825","id":"20210610-042619_599441245","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1399"},{"title":"Define the haversine function","text":"%spark\n\ndef haversine(lat1: Double, lon1: Double, lat2: Double, lon2: Double): Int = {\n        val latDistance = Math.toRadians(lat2 - lat1)\n        val lngDistance = Math.toRadians(lon2 - lon1)\n        val sinLat = Math.sin(latDistance / 2)\n        val sinLng = Math.sin(lngDistance / 2)\n        val a = sinLat * sinLat +\n        (Math.cos(Math.toRadians(lat1)) *\n            Math.cos(Math.toRadians(lat2)) *\n            sinLng * sinLng)\n        val c = 2 * Math.atan2(Math.sqrt(a), Math.sqrt(1 - a))\n        (6371 * 1000 * c).toInt // Average radius of earth in km\n    }","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195708_-2010520956","id":"20210614-190254_449996867","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:03-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:04-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1400"},{"title":"Test the Scala function","text":"%spark\n\nhaversine(36.12, -86.67, 33.94, -118.40)  // = 2887259.9506071107","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:05-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195709_1340107302","id":"20210610-043006_1412529659","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:05-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:06-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1401"},{"title":"Register the Scala function as a UDF","text":"%spark\n\n//val haversine_udf = udf(haversine(_,_,_,_)) // Error (missing parameter type for expanded function)\n\nval haversine_udf = udf((lat1: Double, lon1: Double, lat2: Double, lon2: Double) => \n  haversine(lat1, lon1, lat2, lon2)\n)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:06-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195711_1910988695","id":"20210610-043318_1494705441","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:06-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:07-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1402"},{"title":"Apply the haversine UDF","text":"%spark\n\nval distances = (rides\n  .withColumn(\"haversine_approximation\", haversine_udf($\"origin_lat\", $\"origin_lon\", $\"dest_lat\", $\"dest_lon\"))\n  .select(\"distance\", \"haversine_approximation\"))\ndistances.show(5)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:07-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195712_-457059565","id":"20210610-043404_145411034","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:07-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:09-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1403"},{"title":"We expect the haversine approximation to be less than the ride distance","text":"%spark\n\n(distances\n  .select((col(\"haversine_approximation\") > col(\"distance\")).alias(\"haversine > distance\"))\n  .groupBy(\"haversine > distance\")\n  .count()\n  .show())\n\n// The null values correspond to cancelled rides:\nrides.filter(col(\"cancelled\") === 1).count()\n\n// The true values reflect the fact that the haversine formula is only an approximation to the great-circle distance:\ndistances.filter(col(\"haversine_approximation\") > col(\"distance\")).show(5)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:09-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195713_-743670459","id":"20210610-043506_1356303268","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:09-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1404"},{"text":"%md\n# Lab\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:15-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195714_370661823","id":"20210609-150527_79851234","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:15-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:15-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1405"},{"title":"1- Create a UDF that extracts the day of the week from a timestamp column","text":"%spark\n\n// Define the Scala function:\nimport java.sql.Timestamp\ndef day_of_week(time: Timestamp) : Int = return time.getDay\n\n// Register the Scala function as a UDF: \n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{udf}\nval day_of_week_udf = udf((t: Timestamp) => day_of_week(t))\n\n// Apply the UDF:\nrides_clean.select($\"date_time\", day_of_week_udf($\"date_time\")).show(5, false)\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:16-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195715_1593466262","id":"20210610-044141_285955384","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:16-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1406"},{"title":"Hint","text":"%md\nUse the [weekday](https://docs.python.org/2/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime.weekday) method of the Python `datetime` class.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195716_-957277734","id":"20210610-044216_1671051028","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1407"},{"title":"2 - Use the UDF to compute the number of rides by day of week","text":"%spark\n\n(rides_clean\n  .withColumn(\"day_of_week\", day_of_week_udf($\"date_time\"))\n  .groupBy(\"day_of_week\")\n  .count()\n  .orderBy(\"day_of_week\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195717_285896537","id":"20210610-044215_1321572347","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:18-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:21-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1408"},{"title":"3 - Use the built-in function `dayofweek` to compute the number of rides by day of week","text":"%spark\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{dayofweek}\n\n(rides_clean\n  .withColumn(\"dayofweek\", dayofweek($\"date_time\"))\n  .groupBy(\"dayofweek\")\n  .count()\n  .orderBy(\"dayofweek\")\n  .show())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:21-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195718_977057790","id":"20210610-044211_691709824","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:21-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:24-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1409"},{"text":"%md\n# Result\n**You have now:** Learned how to use UDFs to transform DataFrames\n\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:24-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195719_721192766","id":"20181119-142716_792318228","dateCreated":"2026-11-18T11:29:55-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-18T11:42:24-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-18T11:42:24-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1410"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nDay 1 represents Sunday.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-18T11:42:24-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1795030195725_2105464855","id":"20210610-045022_306202457","date